SOAPBOX: I'm a relative newcomer to CW contests, so I think this was a pretty good effort for me. I had gone into the contest looking for 2 states (WV and AK) to complete my CW WAS. I managed to work AK, but not WV. I was off the air for most of the day Sunday due to family obligations, so 300 QSOs in the log I don't think is too shabby. Aside from breaking the pileup to the AK station with 100 watts and a wire, the highlight of this contest was working WA7BMN on CW for the first time.
SOAPBOX: Thanks to everyone for the QSOs- I had a lot of fun.
